This project reproduces the output of marked (https://github.com/markedjs/marked), version 18.1.3,
and parts of parse.js derive from it:

- the block and inline rule regular expressions (the constants ending in _RE in the two "Rule
  expressions" sections of parse.js, exported as __rules, and the smaller helper expressions
  marked keeps in its "other" rule table, such as the list item, table and escape expressions);
- the parsing algorithm those rules belong to (the order in which rules are tried, the handling of
  block quotes, lists, link reference definitions, emphasis delimiters and autolinks), which
  parse.js follows so that its HTML is identical to marked's.

